    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Stunning four-bedroom end-of-terrace home with a double-height extension and sunny gardens.  This amazing property features a paved driveway leading to an inviting entrance hall, which enjoys solid wood flooring and convenient understairs storage.\r\n\r\nTo the left of the hallway is a spacious, dual-aspect, light-filled living room, featuring a solid fuel/wood burning stove and solid wood flooring. Through French double doors, the living room provides access to the charming patio and sunny rear garden, making this an ideal space to relax with family and entertain friends.\r\n\r\nThe solid wood flooring is carried throughout the downstairs, and the property is completed by an open-plan dining room and kitchen. The L-shaped kitchen enjoys ample counter and cupboard space, as well as additional storage to the rear. The sunny rear garden can also be accessed directly from the kitchen. Upstairs consists of four generously sized bedrooms, one of which is currently being utilised as a spacious home office. The front bedroom also benefits from a stira to access the attic, which is insulated and fully floored, providing additional storage space. The property is completed by a fully tiled family bathroom, enjoying a walk-in electric shower, under sink storage and well-kept sanitary ware.\r\n\r\n150 Tyrconnell Park benefits from its convenient location close to Inchicore Village, where there is a host of services and amenities including cafés, restaurants, supermarkets, gyms and parks.  The location offers the perfect blend of convenience to the city and calm emanating from the numerous green spaces in the area. There is a frequent bus service to the city centre, while the Blackhorse LUAS stop is only a short walk away. The upgraded cycle path along the Grand Canal, the nearby Memorial Gardens and Phoenix Park are all within easy reach offering plenty of scenic walks and recreation. The new children's hospital at St. James's is also close by.\r\n\r\nFeatures:\r\nYear of construction 1935\r\nDouble height extension \r\nGFCH \r\nSolid fuel stove/wood burner\r\nHome office \r\nDual aspect \r\nOpen plan \r\nPaved driveway \r\nSought after location \r\nSunny gardens"
      },
